<b>Nono
Hiiragi</b>

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.230
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.360
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.820
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.030
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.160
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.450
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.450
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.450
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.450
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.450
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.960
<b><i>Bubuki/Buranki</i></b>

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.430
<i>This is Kamakura City Hall's 
Department of Civil Protection.</i>

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:47.770
<i>Citizens of all areas of Kamakura 
are advised to evacuate.</i>

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.770
<i>Please follow instructions from
police and government officials.</i>

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.030
You really only worked with us to kill time?

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.760
Damn it...

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.280
There! That's it! That's it!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.740
That face! That expression!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.290
That's my absolute favorite thing!

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.410
There's some reason
for this, right, Horino-san?

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:14.210
Oh, what a surprise.
I'm impressed you figured that out.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.630
You do! You do have one, don't you?

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.520
I'm sorry. I can't give you 
the details right now.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:23.890
But my true goal is...

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.960
To obtain eternal youth!

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.340
What are you so mad about?

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.570
All I did was tell the truth.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.170
Hiiragi! Calm down!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.690
First, figure out what 
her Bubuki's power is!

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.910
I don't need you to tell me that!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.580
Do you have time to be that cautious?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.050
Did you forget about the Buranki 
heading toward Kamakura?

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:54.920
Shut up. You think I'm going 
to let you provoke me?

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.380
Then I'll just tell you.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.310
My Bubuki can manipulate time.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:05.390
But only for an instant...

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.390
And it's only effective 
in my immediate area.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.480
Now that I've spelled it out,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.400
even you should be able to
 hold your own, right, Hiiragi?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.020
Horino-san, why?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.700
Hmm... This feeling...

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.780
What are you so afraid of?

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.200
You're so indecisive.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.240
Just like your father.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.750
Don't compare me to that loser!

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.380
Yes, that was just an afterimage of me.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.670
You really do love to 
be deceived, don't you?

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.500
Hiiragi!

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:53.730
Oh, dear! Having Iwatooshi 
protect you now, Hiiragi?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.310
A Bubuki's troubles never cease when 
its master is only half a man.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.230
You're not even good for killing time.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:09.580
And I couldn't bear it if my future 
Bubuki, Iwatooshi, were to be broken.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.980
Well, you've done your best for an 
ordinary boy, but this ends that.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.980
Just go to sleep now, Hiiragi.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.000
Damn it... Damn it!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.470
Hiiragi!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.090
He's here.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.890
Hey, you're late, Akihito-kun!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.580
So we've already had two losses?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.810
We're in a tight spot.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.400
I'm back!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:49.040
Sorry about that.
Matobai-san and I kinda blew it.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.280
Good grief.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.410
Souya-kun, are you really sorry?

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.620
Not in the least!

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.810
Honestly... This is problematic.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.940
You don't seem to understand 
the position we're in.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.590
You think so?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.830
It was expected that we'd 
end up two and two, right?

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.800
It looks like Hazama-san's 
duel is pretty much over,

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.640
and no matter who you're up against, 
you'll win like it's nothing.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.640
Like it's nothing, eh?

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.650
I only hope it will be that easy.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.640
Oh, come on. When you're that modest, 
you're just being a smart-ass.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.100
You're a battle genius, aren't you?

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:30.400
But it appears they have a battle 
genius on their side, too.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.770
A battle genius?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.140
Nyo, nyo, nyo?

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.110
Honya?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.070
Over here.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.830
I'll just take that back.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.830
Akihito-kun is being pushed back?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.050
Hey, what the hell is wrong with that girl?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:23.930
Shizuru?

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.290
That's Shizuru-chan... right?

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:43.270
I see.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.900
That's Hiiragi's dad, isn't it?

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.250
Seriously? Hiiragi's daddy 
walks him to and from school?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.740
No way!

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:07.650
Wasn't Hiiragi's dad a friend 
of Kazuki Migiwa, the witch?

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.620
Hey, don't call her a witch.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.500
He'll flip out on you.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:17.270
Damn... Genma and I were 
both used and thrown aside.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.640
I guess, to her,

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:24.020
we're barely worthy to be its sandals,
let alone its limbs.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:29.420
Kazuki Migiwa...
The damned witch who ruined my life...

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:35.060
Hey, Hiiragi. Don't wander off alone.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.370
What are you doing to your father?

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.500
Father?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:48.040
I don't need a loser who drinks 
from sunup to sundown lecturing me!

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.190
What do... What do you know?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:55.560
You call your former ally a witch?

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:59.390
Didn't you and Kazuki Migiwa 
fight Reoko together?!

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:02.310
And yet... And yet...

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.520
Damn! I don't want to know how a 
man who gave up on fighting feels!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:08.940
I don't want to understand!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:12.750
You just follow me around 
like a turd following a goldfish!

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:15.110
And you think you're protecting me?!

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.990
You're pissing me off!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.650
I'm not a little kid anymore!

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.150
What is this picture?

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.490
Hey. Where are you looking?

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.360
I'm... I'm not done yet!

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.780
You should watch, too.
It's not every day you see

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.940
a battle between two geniuses.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:14.070
Genius... Shizuru, a genius?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:18.970
<b>Episode 6
The Gray Jewel</b>

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:27.030
Reoko-sama! Reoko-sama!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.040
Reoko-sama!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.230
This mansion's way too damn big.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.220
Reoko-sama?

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.930
What's this about?

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:50.780
Milk.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.410
Milk is nutritious.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.070
Reoko-sama...

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.970
Milk makes your bones strong.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:08.480
What the hell happened to—

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:12.730
Shuusaku...

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.440
We have a Buranki to eliminate.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.150
R-Right...

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.320
How long was I unconscious?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.290
About two hours.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.080
I brought you from Shinjuku 
here to Kamakura in that time.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.910
And the headless Buranki?

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.100
It began acting autonomously 
only minutes ago.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.380
And Entei?

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:41.700
I'm having it brought to Kamakura via the 
Chuo Depot on the Buranki transport line.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.140
It'll be here at the Banryuu 
stop in about 20 minutes.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.920
We can't wait. We'll go out to meet it.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.100
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.890
Also, I must apologize.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.940
Those brats hit a weak 
spot I never expected.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.110
I will make up for this mistake.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:03.250
Shuusaku, I have only one thing to say.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.030
See that you do.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.030
Foccacia, nusstorte, Sally Lunn...

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:11.990
Foccacia, nusstorte, Sally Lunn...

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.020
Foccacia, nusstorte, Sally Lunn...

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.460
So beautiful...

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.320
Huhwha? Aww...

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:23.510
Forgive me.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:28.850
Sniffle...

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.300
Awesome, Shizuru-chan!

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:34.190
She's been hiding this power 
from us all this time?

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:35.660
Why...

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.430
Good grief.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.560
Show a bit of restraint.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:49.830
Do you intend to burn your 
beloved allies up along with me?

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:54.730
Allies? Allies... Allies...

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:56.340
How very sad.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.840
The stone that once emitted 
only the most brilliant light

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:03.740
seems to have completely lost its shine.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.520
It's been a long time, Shizuru-kun.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.850
Or should I say, "Pleased to meet you"?

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.620
I appreciate this, Aki-kun.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.980
I'm ashamed to say it, but this has 
proven more than I can handle.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:25.800
Not at all. I only hope I can 
be of help to you, my sister.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:31.940
I don't know what's so fun about drawing 
the same picture over and over.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:36.290
She's my own child,
but it just creeps me out.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.800
Shizuru-kun?

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:46.770
I'm your mother's younger brother,
Tsuwabuki Akihito.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.680
Shizuru-kun, I saw the drawings you made.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.640
I'm no expert in the arts,

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.060
so I can't give any expert opinions.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:59.040
But something about your 
pictures attracts me.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:03.660
I'd like to see more of the world you draw.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:30.550
What?

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.630
<b>I</b>

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.250
"I"?

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:55.200
<i>"I cannot become a living thing 
that loves its mother and father."</i>

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.790
Because I am not a living thing.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:05.210
If you're not a living thing,
 then what are you?

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:09.260
I think I am a stone.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:14.670
But my mother and father 
want a normal child.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.960
They want a human.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.070
They don't need a stone.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:33.810
Seeing such outstanding talent 
can make people feel uneasy.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:38.630
So you should forgive
your parents' fear and confusion.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:44.750
And you don't need to force yourself to 
be human just so people will like you.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:49.030
If you think of yourself as a stone,

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.460
you should polish that stone without fear.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:58.080
When you do, you'll be a unique stone 
that shines with a beautiful light.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.480
<b>Nothing</b>

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.720
Foccacia, nusstorte, Sally Lunn...

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.880
Foccacia, nusstorte, Sally Lunn...

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.990
Foccacia...

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.070
What's that?

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:22.870
The Buranki!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.210
What?!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.670
Oh, crap. This is no time 
for a Bubuki battle!

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.810
What's with that Buranki? 
Where's its head?

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:34.510
Shizuru-chan! Stop! You have to Stop!

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:37.560
A-chan...

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:41.500
Kogane-chan, Kinoa, your Rinzu!
Put up your Rinzu!

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.690
<b>Warning
Approaching obstacle. Reduce speed.</b>

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.730
Sorry, Azuma!

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.190
It's okay.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.820
A-chan, I'm sorry!

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.150
I'm really sorry!

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.040
I'm fine.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:13.050
Crap! That giant intends to stomp Oubu flat!

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:20.000
Shizuru-kun, why do you 
fight alongside those four?

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:23.620
They don't try to understand 
who you really are.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:27.440
They're people who only want to use you.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:33.100
Your talent was clouded by the 
fingerprints of people like them.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.750
You are not a beautifully shining stone now.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.750
Wha—

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:47.880
If you're like that,

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:51.180
you won't be able to understand 
your own Bubuki anymore.

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.860
Shizuru! Don't listen to anything he says!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.860
Fight! Fight him!

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.860
That's my order as your leader!

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:23.120
You can't shine if you stay 
with ordinary people like him.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.530
Looks like the duel is over!

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:28.280
Damn...

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:31.670
Shizuru is quite the little bomb, though.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:35.970
That's some teammate you've 
got there, Hiiragi.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.390
She's not a bomb.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:40.340
Huh?

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.510
Shizuru is not a bomb!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.740
She just has more power than she can wield!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:49.770
That's why I have to use 
that thing properly!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:55.280
Hazama Zetsubi, I'm going to 
defeat you, right here and now!

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:00.780
Save the sleep talking for when 
you're asleep, little boy.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.540
A loser will always be a loser.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.590
Life's always so hard on you, isn't it?

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:11.760
At least have a nice dream, Hiiragi.

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:18.180
Hey, can I ask you something, little fool?

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:21.690
I'm telling you that I'll ease your 
pain out of the goodness of my heart.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:23.660
So what do you hope to achieve by

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:28.310
acting tough with a body that won't 
even move the way you want anymore?

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:30.980
Shut up, you hag.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.810
Farewell, Leader-san.

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.020
Oops, too bad.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:50.540
I've already seen through the trick 
of pretending you can't move.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:54.040
I don't like using teleportation, you know.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.110
It dries out my skin.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:57.850
You hag...

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.550
What?

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.320
I called you a hag, you hag!

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.200
This is the problem with children.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:08.560
If you get mad over every little thing, 
no woman will put up with you.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:13.180
That last teleport gave you a 
few new wrinkles, didn't it?

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:17.570
I mean, you've been using it 
over and over, Granny Zetsubi!

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:22.090
I was going to take my time tormenting you,

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.450
but if you're in such a hurry to die...

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.730
This will finish it!

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:34.750
You fall so easily for the 
same trick every single time.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.350
Now! Do it, Iwatooshi!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.600
No!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.770
Too late!

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:00.580
That was a pretty cute 
little squeal, Horino...

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:02.400
I mean, Zetsubi!

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:08.000
Damned spear! Hold back a little, would you?

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.660
I thought my spine was gonna snap.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:15.370
Still, you did as I ordered, Iwatooshi.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.270
I can't believe you got the drop on me...

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:24.420
How does it feel to be taken for a fool,

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.360
Zetsubi?!

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.480
You little shit!

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.060
This is...

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:33.560
I never dreamed Zetsubi-san would lose.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:39.130
Shizuru-kun, sadly, it appears 
we've lost the Bubuki battle.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:44.130
And it would seem your companions 
are not ordinary people, after all.

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:47.060
Now, then...

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:52.830
We need to buy some time 
before Reoko-sama arrives.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.080
A-chan!

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:05.970
A-chan! A-chan!

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:09.270
A-chan!
